## Rotating Card – CSS + HTML

Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows a card (a `<div>` with some content) that rotates 180 deg around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣ Card container ---------- */
.card {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  perspective: 1000px;          /* gives a 3D effect */
  margin: 50px auto;            /* center horizontally */
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣ Card inner wrapper ---------- */
.card__inner {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  position: relative;
  transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* smooth rotation */
  transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* keep children in 3D space */
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣ Front & Back faces ---------- */
.card__face {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;      /* hide back side when turned */
  border-radius: 10px;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.2);
}

.card__face--front {
  background: #fff;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: #333;
}

.card__face--back {
  background: #4a90e2;
  color: #fff;
  transform: rotateY(180deg);       /* start flipped */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣ Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover .card__inner {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);        /* flip on hover */
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card__inner">
    <div class="card__face card__face--front">
      Front Side
    </div>
    <div class="card__face card__face--back">
      Back Side
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| 1️⃣ | `.card` sets `perspective` | Gives depth to the 3D rotation. |
| 2️⃣ | `.card__inner` holds the two faces | `transform-style: preserve-3d` keeps children in 3D space. |
| 3️⃣ | Two faces (`front` & `back`) | `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the back when it’s facing away. |
| 4️⃣ | Hover on `.card` → rotate inner wrapper | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` flips the card. |

Feel free to replace the text, colors, or add more content inside the faces.  
If you want a different axis (e.g., X‑axis) just change `rotateY` to `rotateX`.
